<title>GERMANY: Siemens recovers on Philips profit warning.</title>
<headline>Siemens recovers on Philips profit warning.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in German electronic giant Siemens AG recovered from earlier lows in bourse trade after the Dutch electronics group Philips issued a surprise profit warning.</p>
<p>Siemens shares were up five pfennigs in mid-session bourse trade at 80.55 marks, having fallen to 80.18 marks at one point earlier in the session.</p>
<p>The overall DAX index was up 0.30 percent at 2,694.05 points.</p>
<p>Shares in Philips Electronic NV fell by more than five percent after the group revised its profit outlook for the second half of the year downwards.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
